    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_open">About CityPulse</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s · Academic project</string>
    <string name="about_intro">CityPulse shows you what\'s happening right now in the city: concerts, markets, fairs and culture a few minutes\' walk from where you are.</string>
    <string name="about_data_title">WHERE THE DATA COMES FROM</string>
    <string name="about_data_tm">Ticketmaster: concerts, shows and ticket sales.</string>
    <string name="about_data_catalog">Our own catalog (Firebase): markets, fairs and free plans. It\'s demo data; times and prices may not match reality.</string>
    <string name="about_data_osm">Maps © OpenStreetMap contributors. Walking, cycling and driving routes computed with OSRM (FOSSGIS server).</string>
    <string name="about_data_images">Sample images from Unsplash. Voice navigation with Google Maps.</string>
    <string name="about_ai_title">ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE</string>
    <string name="about_ai_body">Search, summaries and Surprise sentences use Google\'s Gemini. The AI only interprets what you write and drafts text: events always come from real data. It can be wrong; check the event details before going.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">YOUR DATA</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Your location is used on the phone to calculate distances and isn\'t stored on any server; only when you open the route to an event is it sent, together with the destination, to the OSRM routing server (FOSSGIS) to compute the path. Your preferences stay on the device. So do your saved events, unless you sign in: then they\'re copied to your Firebase (Google) account along with your name and email, so you can see them on other phones. You can delete everything in Your account → Delete account. What you type in the AI search and the information of the events you summarize is sent to Google to be processed.</string>
    <string name="about_osm_link">OpenStreetMap license</string>
    <string name="about_code_link">Source code on GitHub</string>

